upcie-experimental (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Track upcie 0.9.0.
  * dmabuf_import: DMABUF_IMPORT_ATTACH_BDF imports now belong to the open
    device file and are freed when it is closed. Callers must keep the device
    open for as long as they use the addresses.
  * dmabuf_import: attach and the lookups refuse a descriptor number that has
    come to name a different buffer with ESTALE, where they used to answer
    with the standing import's addresses; DETACH still takes it. Unloading the
    module now releases the imports the DMABUF_IMPORT_ATTACH table still
    holds, and that ioctl logs a deprecation warning naming the caller.

 -- Simon A. F. Lund <os@safl.dk>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 18:04:59 +0200

upcie-experimental (0.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of the merged package: ship dmabuf_import and iommu_map_pa
    in one binary package, since the experimental paths need both. Supersedes
    dmabuf-import-dkms (0.2.0) and iommu-map-pa-dkms (0.2.0), which are
    conflicted, replaced and provided.
  * Track the upcie version rather than versioning the modules separately, so
    the deb, the DKMS tree, MODULE_VERSION and the upcie headers all agree.
  * Load both modules on install and on boot; mask
    /usr/lib/modules-load.d/upcie-experimental.conf to opt out.

 -- Simon A. F. Lund <os@safl.dk>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:25:59 +0200
